 "method_html": "\n<h3>Team strength</h3>\n<p>Opponent-adjusted <strong>EPA per play</strong> on offense and defense (nflverse play-by-play), fit by weighted ridge regression each week. Recent games count more (0.93\u00d7 per week of age), garbage time is excluded (win probability outside 5\u201395%), and ratings are shrunk toward 50% of last season's values so early weeks stay stable. Net EPA/play \u00d7 62 plays converts to points.</p>\n<h3>Elo</h3>\n<p>A 538-style Elo from game results since 2009 (K=20, margin-of-victory multiplier, \u2153 regression each off-season), 25 Elo points per point of spread.</p>\n<h3>Quarterbacks</h3>\n<p>Each starter's EPA per dropback (this season, last season at 70%, two seasons ago at 40%), shrunk toward replacement level (250 dropbacks of prior). The starter listed in the nflverse schedule is compared with the QB play the team's ratings were built on; the difference \u00d7 35 dropbacks moves the line (capped at \u00b19). Backup starts are the biggest single adjustment in the model.</p>\n<h3>Projection</h3>\n<p>Margin = 7% EPA + 93% Elo + QB adjustment + 1.5 points home field (none at neutral sites) + a small rest term (0.05 pts/day, capped; post-2011 rest effects are near zero). Cover probability uses a margin distribution reweighted to real NFL final margins since 2005, so key numbers like 3 and 7 carry their true weight and pushes are priced.</p>\n<h3>Picks, confidence and tuning</h3>\n<p>Edge = projected margin vs the line. Backtests show the model's gap to the line hasn't predicted results, so bets are priced at a market-anchored line that moves 15% of the way from the line toward the model, at most 1.5 points. Tiers come from expected value at that price: lean above 0%, play 1.5%+, strong 3%+. Cover chances use a margin distribution with real key-number frequencies (3, 7, 10...), starting from the margin that makes the line a coin flip. Over/unders are priced the same way. Confidence (0\u2013100) weighs whether EPA and Elo each cover on their own, edge, line movement, ATS trends, and data quality (games played, known starting QBs). After each week the EPA/Elo weights and home field are refit to this season's results and moved part of the way there.</p>\n<p>Data: <a href=\"https://github.com/nflverse\">nflverse</a> (CC BY 4.0) schedules, lines and play-by-play. For entertainment only.</p>",
